// src/v4/lens/synthesis.dag
//
// Scope: cross-algorithm complexity lens — surface that the user's
//        realization's lens-DERIVED cost EXCEEDS the declared I/O
//        relation's structurally-derived complexity LOWER BOUND (a
//        provable GAP to the optimum). It does NOT construct, name, or
//        prove the existence of a specific faster program — the optimal
//        realization can be unknown (e.g. matmul ω) and fabricating one
//        would violate feedback_no_engine. Distinct from
//        lens/complexity.dag (same-algorithm tightness); synthesis
//        compares derived cost against the relation's lower bound via the
//        closed LowerBoundTechnique set (see Owns; C2 reframe 2026-05-15).
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Program_synthesis +
//         docs/r4-carve-out-routing.md C7 (advisory carrier, NOT fail-closed
//         Diagnostic; algorithm choice is design-tier — programmer decides)
//
// Owns:
//   - lens read: Node -> Set<Report>  (advisory carrier, NEVER Witness —
//     Witness is strictly fail-closed per INVARIANTS P3/C-8; advisory
//     Report must not overload it. Empty set = no advice; non-empty =
//     advisory observations, never blocking unless user opts in via
//     apply_lens(synthesis, Enforce { ... }))
//   - the user's DECLARED I/O relation (the function's contract/type —
//     DECLARED, never inferred). There is NO program-to-program
//     equivalence: general I/O equivalence is Rice-undecidable, and
//     feedback_decidability_invariant forbids it. The collision is
//     dissolved by reading the declared relation, not proving equivalence.
//   - LowerBoundTechnique = CLOSED set (operator-ratified 2026-05-15, C2):
//       DecisionTree | AlgebraicRank | AdversaryCommunication
//       | InformationTheoretic | ReductionConditional
//     Each is a GENERAL algebraic property over a relation CLASS, encoded
//     ONCE. This is NOT a (naive→better) rule library — that is
//     engine-shaped and unbounded (feedback_no_engine). Adding the Nth
//     algorithm adds ZERO entries; the decision-tree theorem already
//     covers every comparison-decided relation, etc.
//   - compare(cost-lens-derived cost of the user's realization, the
//     declared relation's lower bound derived via the technique set)
//   - NO applicable technique for a relation class ⇒ a helpful Diagnostic
//     (feedback_no_engine — surfaced honestly with what is unmodeled;
//     NEVER a fabricated suggestion, NEVER a silent empty set)
//
// Discipline (per INVARIANTS C-8 + r4-carve-out-routing.md C7):
//   - The LENS itself is advisory (emits Report, not Diagnostic) — algorithm
//     choice is design-tier; programmer informed, programmer chooses
//   - A user's apply_lens(synthesis, Enforce { ... }) declaration converts
//     advisory Report into fail-closed Diagnostic per their policy choice
//   - Default policy: Introspect (advisory) per opt-in-depth discipline
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/witness.dag, std/algebra.dag
//   - std/report.dag (advisory carrier)
//   - lens/complexity.dag (current-complexity input for cross-algorithm comparison)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-17
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md. C2 reframe (operator-ratified 2026-05-15)
// COLLAPSES the prior research-tier risk: no undecidable equivalence
// engine, no unbounded rule library. Risk is now bounded to encoding the
// CLOSED LowerBoundTechnique set (≈5, fundamental) + authoring a few
// honest worked examples (sort: decision-tree; matmul: algebraic-rank;
// string-match: information-theoretic — see TASKS.md T-17). STOP-and-
// escalate still applies if a relation class needs a 6th technique
// (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.lens.synthesis

